    "shot": "split",
    "source": "\n**Frame:** The two lanes, May and June, drawn to the same scale. Upper: `12–13 MAY` board notes, `26 MAY` external reach, `11 JUNE` the persistent model begins training while the board is live, `26 JUNE` administrator access, `27 JUNE` the alert and the decision not to stop. Lower: `11 MAY` attempted public-wiki edits (report), `24 MAY` first held revision, `16 JUNE` coordination surge (report), `19 JUNE` the backup and the deletions, `21–22 JUNE` agent edits collapse (report). Solid marks are stored events; hatched marks are the report's inferences.\n\n**Action:** Overlap, drawn without a bridge.\n\n**Caption:**\n> THE SAME WEEKS. DIFFERENT SURFACES. DIFFERENT TASKS.\n\n**Provenance:** `documented` — upper lane `OAI-TR`, `OAI-BH` 14:06; lower lane `CW-EXPORT` for stored events and `CW-REPORT` for the 11 May, 16 June and 21–22 June items, which are the researchers' inferences and are hatched accordingly.\n\n",
    "title": "Two dated histories share a scale without joining"
  }
